From 79be5c3a74add3726a03783ce5b1378b13c3d41d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hasan Mehdi <hasanthemehdi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:18:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bt: shared volume, Galaxy Buds batteries, the jack asleep on
 Bluetooth

Volume: headphones that report their volume (AVRCP absolute volume) now
share it. We ask what they report, subscribe to their volume, and from the
first (interim) answer on the music goes out at full scale while their
volume sets the loudness; the player's volume keys step it (16 steps,
SetAbsoluteVolume), their own buttons move the same one. Each pair keeps
its volume (bt_devices.txt absvol=); a pair new to us starts no louder
than half way. Headphones without it keep the player's software volume, and
their volume buttons (AVRCP passthrough VOL_UP/DOWN) now act as the player's
volume keys. btc_avrc.c passes interim notifications on, flagged.

Batteries: Galaxy Buds tell theirs over Samsung's RFCOMM service
2e73a4ad-332d-41fc-90e2-16bef06523f2 (format as documented by
GalaxyBudsClient). buds.c finds the channel with BTA JV's SDP discovery,
opens it, reads status messages 0x61/0x60 (left, right, case, placement)
and answers the first with "manager info". RFCOMM runs through BTA JV
without the SPP profile (it needs FreeRTOS ring buffers and a VFS);
bta_jv_act.c had all its includes under BTA_JV_L2CAP_INCLUDED.

Power: while audio is on Bluetooth the headphone amp sleeps (shutdown pin,
output muted first) and the DAC gets no I2S clocks (HAVE_WIRED_SLEEP);
they wake before the jack plays again. Sniff/active mode changes are
logged to bt.log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
